    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξαλλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>special, distinguishing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσθῆτες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.7.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ki.</u>
				6.14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					737.19
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στολαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.468
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἔ. τοῦ βαρβαρικοῦ κόσμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.330a
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span>
			<i>strangely,</i> of superstitious veneration, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				32.15.7
			</span></i>.</div>
